{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#109","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#109","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#109\",\"parent_revision\":\"642eb29ec08ee0f45ac9896a0f6fbaac329ede5121113ca3d28efb3af32c10ea\",\"root_revision\":\"642eb29ec08ee0f45ac9896a0f6fbaac329ede5121113ca3d28efb3af32c10ea\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nPR #108 scoped the AS family to `SKILL.md` only. The AgentSkills specification is a cross-harness baseline for **skills** \u2014 it defines `SKILL.md` and does not describe agent files at all, so AS rules evaluating `agents/*.md` were a category error by construction.\\n\\nThat was the right boundary, but it leaves a real gap, correctly flagged in automated review on that PR.\\n</div>\\n\\n## The Gap\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAS007 (wildcard tool entries) and AS008 (MCP server name casing) were the **only** checks covering an agent's `tools:` field. With the AS family scoped to skills, `agents/*.md` now gets no tools-field validation at all.\\n\\nConcretely, this passes lint today:\\n\\n```yaml\\n---\\nname: broken\\ndescription: ...\\ntools: mcp__*\\n---\\n```\\n\\nPer `code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-agents.md`:\\n\\n> If no entry in the list resolves to a tool, the subagent usually fails to launch with an error naming the entries.\\n\\nSo that agent cannot launch, and nothing warns about it.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Why It Wasn T Fixed In 108\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`tools:` is Claude Code subagent frontmatter. A rule for it belongs in a series that governs agent files, cited to the harness documentation that defines them. Creating that series means choosing a new code prefix and its authority model \u2014 a design decision, not a bugfix, and out of scope for a PR whose purpose was removing false rationales.\\n\\nAS007 still exists in its corrected form but is now effectively dead for its original target: it checks a Claude Code field from a family that no longer runs on Claude Code agent files.\\n</div>\\n\\n## What Needs Deciding\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n1. **A series that governs agent files** \u2014 new prefix, authority cited to `code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-agents.md`.\\n2. **AS007's fate** \u2014 port its corrected logic into that series and delete it from AS, or delete it outright.\\n3. **AS008 likewise** \u2014 MCP server-name casing applies to agent `tools:` and to skill `allowed-tools`; it may need to exist in both places with different authorities.\\n4. **Audit the rest of the AS family** for other rules reading fields the AgentSkills spec does not define. AS002 already carried a hand-written agent-file suppression before the boundary existed, so this pattern has precedent.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `docs/design-rule-provenance-registry.md` specifies the Rule \u2192 Claim \u2192 Authority pipeline that would prevent a rule citing an authority that does not cover its field. `packages/skilllint/schemas/provenance-registry.json` does not exist yet.\\n- 25 rules (hk 5, pl 6, pr 5, pd 3, lk 2, nr 2, sl 1, tc 1) currently have an `origin` and no `reference` after #108 removed a dead link. They are the concrete backlog for that registry.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"f90e8aab3d6e9bd9aa3a21554be35ff3c4afa8c7d156e1f23ffd119becad693e\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDORXxKvc8AAAABXP-tOQ\"}"}